#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065389 :tutorial/content "We can use differentiation to solve related rates problems in the context of cones. In general, we follow the usual three steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Draw a diagram and identify the variables that change with time.\n\n**Step 2:** Write down a relation between the time-dependent variables.\n\n**Step 3:** Differentiate the relation with respect to time and plug in the known values.\n\nBefore we start, recall that the volume $v$ of a right cone of radius $r$ and height $h$ (shown below) is given by the formula\n\n$$\nv = \\dfrac13 \\pi r^2 h\n$$\n\n![](images/cf/cf4e3b5b9f0d827bccaee008e006ad62d870fb2d782df8dd94f61bc4a3ca4050.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "312c7731-2fba-5fc2-9a6b-e551caf483da" :tutorial/math-academy-id 505 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
